      "id": "2-rome-late-antiquity",
      "title": "Rome & Late Antiquity",
      "description": "From Lucretius to Boethius: natural philosophy, engineering, and empire under the Roman peace, ending in the long twilight of the ancient world. The Bible is read in stations across the section, and classical mathematics opens here with Diophantus — met in its own terms, to be taken up by the algebra of the eras ahead.",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "holy-bible-kjv",
          "note": "The Bible is read in five stations across this section; begin here with the Law.",
