          "note": "The Greek thread closes here; the translation exercises point onward for those who continue. The New Testament itself arrives later in the section."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "diophantus-arithmetica",
          "note": "A long-runner, like Euclid before it — two or three problems a day alongside the rest. Read him in his own terms; the supplement shows what his notation actually looked like, and why Heath's page reads as modern algebra.",
          "passages": [
            "Book I: the Preliminary; then Problems 1–39",
            "Book II",
            "Book III, Problems 10–16",
            "Book IV, Problems 1–2, 10–11, 18, 24–28",
